openi2pd state directory
========================

This directory holds the router's keys, netDb, profiles, torrents and the
default pidfile for the OpenBSD service. Keep it owned by `_i2pd` with mode
0700 and do not edit files here that are managed by the daemon.

This README is also the package marker that makes the PLIST `@sample` entry
create `/var/i2pd`; leave it in place. The packaged configuration samples are
installed under /etc/i2pd; see pkg_info -D i2pd and the pkg-readme for the
service paths.
